<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#primogeniture">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Primogeniture</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Primogeniture is the rule of inheritance by which the eldest son succeeds to the whole of a title or estate. Its absence often led to succession disputes. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a> had no law of primogeniture, so each sultan's death triggered civil war among his heirs, and the lack of strict primogeniture in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rozvi-empire">Rozvi Empire</a> also produced recurring disputes.</p></div>
